    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW29f7oazwAC2Eh51x1XcYfuA)_\n\n## What\n\n`consult-omni/:config: Cannot open load file: elfeed`: every consult-omni source requires the package it searches (`elfeed`, `notmuch`, `consult-gh`, `consult-mu`). The loader uses `(require symbol nil t)`, but NOERROR only covers the source file itself, not what it requires in turn, so one missing package aborted the whole `:config`. `sp-consult-omni-load-module` now replaces the loader's `consult-omni-sources--load-module` and skips such a source with a message in `*Messages*`. Install the package to get the source. Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not changed: tooltips warning\n\nThe #202 recipe does link `tooltips.css`/`tooltips.js` next to the library (Elpaca links the files of `:files` by name into the build folder), but Elpaca does not relink an already built package when its recipe changes. Run `M-x elpaca-rebuild RET org-special-block-extras` and restart.\n\n## Tested\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9DjJ1RiaewzjEB2R6)_",
    "changed_files": 3,
    "closed_at": "2026-10-31T16:44:11Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "OWNER",
            "body": "The `tangle` check fails only on `libraries/modules/custom/sp-thesis-dump.el`, which this PR does not touch: `main` has an edit of that file that its doc does not have. #205 removes the file and untangles the doc, which fixes it. The `sp-browsing` doc and `.el` of this PR agree, so nothing to change here; the check should pass once #205 is merged and this branch is updated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
